"hadiths[42]{hadithnumber,text}:"
488,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:the Prophet said: ""The best day that the sun has risen upon is Friday. On it Adam was created"
489,"Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Seek out the hour that is hoped for on Friday after Asr until the sun has set"
490,"Kathir bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Awf Al-Muzani narrated from his father"
491,"Abu Hurairah narrated:""Allah's Messenger said: The best day that the sun has risen upon is Friday. On it Adam was created"
492,"It was narrated to us by Ahmad ibn Mani', who narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Whoever attends the Friday prayer, let him perform Ghusl (ritual bath)."" He said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Umar, Abu Sa'id, Jabir, Al-Bara', Aishah, and Abu Ad-Darda'. Abu Isa said: The Hadith of Ibn Umar is a Hasan (good) and Sahih (authentic) Hadith."
493,"Salim narrated:(Another chain) from Abdullah bin Umar from the Prophet which is similar"
494,"Abū ʿĪsā said: It has also been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar, from ʿUmar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday. This is a hasan sahih hadith. It was narrated by Yūnus and Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father: While ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was delivering the sermon on Friday, a man from among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered. ʿUmar asked, ""What time is this [that you have come]?"" The man replied, ""I only heard the call to prayer, and I did no more than perform ablution (wuḍūʾ)."" ʿUmar said, ""And [only] ablution? You know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded [us] to perform the ritual bath (ghusl)."" Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Abān narrated this to us, from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī."
495,"(Another chain reaching to Az-Zuhri) with this Hadith.Malik reported this Hadith from Az-Zuhri"
496,"Aws bin Aws narrated:""Allah's Messenger said to me: 'Whoever performs Ghusl on Friday"
497,"Samurah bin Jundah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: ""Whoever performs Wudu on Friday"
498,"Abu Hurairh narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: ""Whoever performs Wudu"
499,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: ""Whoever performs Ghusl on Friday - the Ghusl for Janabah - then he goes"
500,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by ʿAlī ibn Khashram:** He informed us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus reported from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from ʿAbīdah ibn Sufyān, from Abū al-Jaʿd — meaning al-Ḍamrī — who was, as Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr claimed, a Companion (ṣāḥābī). He said:

**The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:**

> *""Whoever abandons the Friday prayer (Jumuʿah) three times out of negligence, Allah will set a seal upon his heart.""*

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** There are narrations on this topic from Ibn ʿUmar, Ibn ʿAbbās, and Samurah.

**Abū ʿĪsā said:** The hadith of Abū al-Jaʿd is a *ḥasan* (good) hadith.

**He further said:** I asked Muḥammad (i.e., Imām al-Bukhārī) regarding the name of Abū al-Jaʿd al-Ḍamrī, but he did not know his name. He said: *""I do not know of any narration from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, from him other than this hadith.""*

**Abū ʿĪsā said:** And we do not know of this hadith except through the narration of Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr.

---

*Reference: Sunan al-Tirmidhī, Kitāb al-Ṣalāh, Bāb mā jā'a fī tark al-Jumuʿah.*"
501,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by 'Abd ibn Humayd and Muhammad ibn Maddūyah** — they both said: **Fadl ibn Dukayn** narrated to us: **Isrā'īl** narrated to us, from **Thuwayr**, from **a man from the people of Qubā'**, from **his father**, who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, who said:

> ""The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to attend the Friday prayer (al-Jumu'ah) from Qubā'.""

**It has also been narrated from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ regarding this matter, but it is not authentic (lā yasihh).**

**Abū 'Īsā** (al-Tirmidhī) commented: *""This hadith is not known except through this chain of narration, and nothing authentic (lā yasihh) has been reported in this chapter from the Prophet ﷺ.""*

He further stated: *""It has been narrated from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said:*

> **'The Friday prayer is obligatory upon one whose night brings him back to his family.'**

*However, this hadith has a weak chain of narration (isnāduhu da'īf); it is only reported through the hadith of Mu'ārik ibn 'Abbād from 'Abd Allāh ibn Sa'īd al-Maqburī.""*

And **Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd al-Qaṭṭān** declared **'Abd Allāh ibn Sa'īd al-Maqburī** to be weak (da'īf) in hadith.

Abū 'Īsā then stated: *""The scholars have differed regarding upon whom the Friday prayer is obligatory. Some of them said: 'The Friday prayer is obligatory upon one whose night brings him back to his dwelling.' Others said: 'The Friday prayer is obligatory only upon one who hears the call (al-nidā')' — and this is the position of **al-Shāfi'ī**, **Aḥmad**, and **Isḥāq**.""*

---

*Note: This narration is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī, and as the author himself clarifies, its chain of narration is considered weak (da'īf) among the scholars of hadith.*"
502,"Narrator not mentioned:I heard Ahmad bin Husain saying: ""We were with Ahmad bin Hanbal"
503,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Prophet would pray the Friday prayer when the sun was declining"
504,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Yahya ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān narrated from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Taymī, from Anas رضي الله عنه, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it.**

He (Abū ʿĪsā) said: **""And in this chapter (there are narrations) from Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ, Jābir, and al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām رضي الله عنهم.""**

Abū ʿĪsā said: **""The ḥadīth of Anas رضي الله عنه is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. It is that upon which the majority of the people of knowledge have reached consensus: that the time for the Jumuʿah prayer is when the sun passes its zenith (zawāl), just like the time of the Ẓuhr prayer. This is the position of al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq.**

**However, some of them held the view that if the Jumuʿah prayer is performed before the sun's zenith, it is also valid. Aḥmad said: 'Whoever prays it before the zawāl, he did not see any obligation upon him to repeat it.'""**

---

*Note: This narration is recorded in Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī and pertains to the chapter on the timing of the Jumuʿah prayer. The chain of narration includes Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī (Ṭaysalān), Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān al-Madanī, ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Taymī, and Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله"
505,"Ibn Umar narrated:""The Prophet would give the Khutbah next to the trunk of a date palm. When he [the Prophet] began using the Minbar the trunk cried out for him until he came to it and held it"
506,"Ibn Umar narrated:""The Prophet would give a Khutbah on Friday"
507,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah and Hannād narrated to us, both saying:** Abū al-Ahwāṣ narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Jābir ibn Samurah رضي الله عنه, who said:

*""I used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, and his prayer was moderate (in length), and his sermon (khutbah) was moderate (in length).""*

He (the narrator) said: **""And in this chapter (there are narrations) from ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir and Ibn Abī Awfā.""**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""The Ḥadīth of Jābir ibn Samurah is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ Ḥadīth.""**

---

### Notes on Translation:

- **قَصْدًا (qasdan):** Translated as ""moderate"" or ""of moderate length,"" indicating that the Prophet ﷺ neither prolonged his prayer nor shortened it excessively, but maintained a balanced, measured approach — a hallmark of his Sunnah in worship.
- **Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ:** This is al-Tirmidhī's grading, indicating that the chain of narration meets the criteria of both *ḥasan* (good) and *ṣaḥīḥ* (authentic), reflecting a high degree of reliability."
508,"Safwan bin Ya'la bin Umayyah narrated from his father who said:""I heard the Prophet reciting"
509,"Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:""When Allah's Messenger descending the Minbar he would face our direction"
510,"Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:""The Prophet was delivering a Khutbah on Friday when a man came. The Prophet said: 'Have you prayed?' He said no. So he said: 'Then stand and pray.'"" Abu Eisa said: This Hadith is Hasan Sahih [It is the most correct thing about this topic]"
511,"Iyad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sarh narrated:""Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri entered (the mosque) on Friday while Marwan was giving the Khutbah"
512,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: ""Whoever said: 'Be quiet' while the Imam is giving the Khutbah then he has committed Laghw (useless activity)"
513,"Sahl bin Ma'adh bin Anas al Jahni narrated from his father that :Allah's Messenger said: ""Whoever steps over the necks of the people on Friday"
514,"Sahl bin Ma'adh narrated from his father:""The Prophet prohibited Al-Habwah on Friday while the Imam is delivering the Khutbah"
515,"Husain narrated:""I heard Umarah bin Rawaibah Ath-Thaqafi - while Bishr bin Marwan was delivering Khutbah and raising his hands in supplication - so Umarah said: 'May Allah disgrace these two insignificant hands"
516,"As-Sa'ib bin Yazid narrated:""The Adhan during the time of Allah's Messenger"
517,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""Allah's Messenger would talk as necessary after descending from the Minbar"
518,"Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Khallāl narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar informed us, from Thābit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said: ""I saw the Prophet ﷺ, after the prayer had been established, being spoken to by a man who stood between him and the qiblah. The man continued speaking to him, and I saw some of us dozing off due to the length of the Prophet's ﷺ standing."" Abū ʿĪsā said: ""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."""
519,"Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi the freed slave of Allah's Messenger said:""Marwan left Abu Hurairah in charge of Al-Madinah and he went to Makkah. So Abu Hurairah led us in Salat in Friday"
520,"Narrated by Ali ibn Hujr, who reported from Sharik, from Mukhawil ibn Rashid, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'eed ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday Surah Al-Sajdah (Surah 32) and Surah Al-Insan (Surah 76).

He (the narrator) said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Sa'd, Ibn Mas'ud, and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them).

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Ibn Abbas is a hasan sahih hadith. It was also narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri, Shu'bah, and others from Mukhawil."
521,"Salim narrated from his father:""The Prophet would pray two Rak;ah after the Friday prayer"
522,"Nafi narrated about Ibn Umar:""When he prayed the Friday prayer"
523,"Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhail bin Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever among you prays after Jumu'ah, let him pray four (units).'""

Abu 'Eisa said: This Hadith is Hasan Sahih.

Al-Hasan bin Ali narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Madini narrated to us, from Sufyan bin 'Uyainah, who said: ""We used to consider Suhail bin Abi Salih to be reliable (thabt) in Hadith.""

This is acted upon by some of the people of knowledge.

It has been narrated from Abdullah bin Mas'ud that he used to pray four (units) before Jumu'ah and four after it.

It has also been narrated from Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he ordered praying two units after Jumu'ah, then four.

Sufyan Ath-Thawri and Ibn Al-Mubarak held the view of Ibn Mas'ud.

Ishaq said: ""If one prays in the masjid on Friday, he should pray four; and if he prays in his house, he should pray two."" He argued that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray two units after Jumu'ah in his house, and (also cited) the Hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ): ""Whoever among you prays after Jumu'ah, let him pray four.""

Abu 'Eisa said: It is Ibn Umar who narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he used to pray two units after Jumu'ah in his house. And Ibn Umar, after the Prophet (ﷺ), used to pray two units in the masjid after Jumu'ah, and after the two units he would pray four.

Ibn Abi Umar narrated that to us, Sufyan bin 'Uyainah narrated to us, from Ibn Juraij, from Ata', who said: ""I saw Ibn Umar pray two units after Jumu'ah, then after that he prayed four.""

Sa'eed bin Abdur-Rahman Al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan bin 'Uyainah narrated to us, from Amr bin Dinar, who said: ""I have not seen anyone more precise in Hadith than Az-Zuhri, and I have not seen anyone for whom dinars and dirhams were more insignificant than for him; dinars and dirhams were, to him, like camel dung.""

Abu 'Eisa said: I heard Ibn Abi Umar say: I heard Sufyan bin 'Uyainah say: ""Amr bin Dinar was older than Az-Zuhri."""
524,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Whoever catches a Rak'ah of the Salat then he has caught the Salat"
525,"Sahl bin Sa'd narrated:""We would not have lunch during the time of Allah's Messenger"
526,"Ibn Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: ""When one of you becomes sleepy during the Friday prayer"
527,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet sent Abdullah bin Rawahah to lead a military detachment"
528,"Al-Bara bin Azib narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: ""It is a duty for the Muslims"
529,"Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:(Another route for the same chain) similar in meaning"
